{"content": " Showing Interest and Surprise", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When someone tells you something you did not expect, you can show interest and surprise.<br /> You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">Really? </span>or <span class=\"italic\">That's interesting!</span> You can change the tone of your voice to show that you are interested or surprised.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Ann</span>: I have something to tell you.<br />  <span class =\"strong\">Bob</span>: Ok \u2026 ? What is it?<br />  <span class =\"strong\">Ann</span>: I bought a one-way ticket to London.<br />  <span class =\"strong\">Bob</span>: You did what?? I didn't see that one coming!<br />", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Showing Interest </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Showing Surprise </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">And \u2026 ? / Ok \u2026 ? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Really? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What is it? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You did what?? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That's interesting! </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you kidding me? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You bet! </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I didn't see that one coming! </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tell ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say something to someone ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have something important to tell you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about a surprise trip!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "one-way ticket ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a ticket to a destination, no return ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I bought a one-way ticket to Paris.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "return ticket ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a ticket to a destination and back ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I bought a return ticket to Mexico. I'm going for a week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to head to ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to leave; to go towards a destination ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm heading to Paris tomorrow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "You bet! ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "You can be sure of it! ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class = \"strong\">Ann</span>: I want to read all about it in your blog! <span class = \"strong\">Bob</span>: You bet!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "culture ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the history, art, etc. of a place ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love French culture!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the Old Continent ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Europe ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to travel around the Old Continent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Are you kidding me? ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Are you serious?; Really? ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class = \"strong\">Ann</span>: I bought a one-way ticket to Paris. <span class = \"strong\">Bob</span>: Are you kidding me?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I didn't see that one coming! ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I wasn't expecting this; I'm surprised ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ann is leaving tomorrow. I didn't see that one coming!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished event or a specific time in the past.<br>  <br>You can form the regular form of the Simple Past tense by adding -ed or -ied to the verb.</br>  <br>We use the auxiliary  <span class =\"strong\">did</span> to make negative and interrogative statements. Look at the chart.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You <span class =\\\"strong\\\">called</span> me last night.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You <span class =\\\"strong\\\">didn't call</span> me last night.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> you <span class =\\\"strong\\\">call</span> me last night?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She  <span class =\\\"strong\\\">wanted</span> a return ticket.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She <span class =\\\"strong\\\">didn't want</span>  a return ticket.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class =\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> she  <span class =\\\"strong\\\">want</span>  a return ticket?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Some verbs are irregular. Their Simple Past form doesn't end in -ed or -ied. Here are some examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">saw</span> you at the station.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">didn't see</span> you at the station.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">see</span> you at the station?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bring\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">brought</span> my passport.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">didn't bring</span> my passport.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">bring</span> my passport?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"buy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">bought</span> a return ticket.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">didn't buy</span> a return ticket.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">buy</span> a return ticket?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of three surprising or interesting things to tell a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2 things are true. 1 thing is false.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your partner expresses surprise each time you say something.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner to guess which one is false. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about surprising things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I show surprise with expressions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I determine what statements are true and which are false.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}